.TITLE "format"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Formats a disk for use with Windows. It prepares a storage medium by creating a new file system and is a critical tool for __disk initialization__.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**format D:**
Formats the specified drive using the default file system.
> __D:__ the target drive letter

**format D: /fs:NTFS**
Formats the drive with a specific file system like NTFS or FAT32.
> __/fs:NTFS__ file system flag

**format D: /v:label**
Specifies the volume label for the formatted disk.
> __/v:label__ volume label flag

**format D: /q**
Performs a quick format by deleting the file table and root directory.
> __/q__ quick format flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using the __/q__ flag is much faster than a standard format but does not scan for bad sectors. Always double-check the drive letter before formatting to avoid accidental __permanent data loss__.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:chkdsk** **windows:dir**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/format__
